  "notes": [
    "`imuTemp` read in kelvin, from the values: they run from 293.4 to 293.87. That is within the 233.15 to 333.15 K an electronics bay can have. In degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit they would be hotter than any bay survives",
    "`accelX`, `accelY` and `accelZ` read in meters per second squared, from the pad's gravity: the three axes' magnitude reads within 10% of 9.806 65 for 20.6 s of the file's time. It reads within 10% of 1 for 0.0 s. A board at rest or under a parachute reads 1 g. The unit whose 1 g lasts at least 1 s and twice as long as the other's is taken",
    "`gyroX`, `gyroY` and `gyroZ` read in radians per second, from the board's turning: over 3 stretches of 10 steps at most 0.05 s apart with the accelerometer within 15% of 1 g, its direction turns 0.600 rad. A board at rest or under a parachute reads so. Over the same stretches, the gyroscope's rates turn the board across that direction 0.600 rad read in radians per second, 0.010 rad read in degrees. The unit whose turn is within a quarter to 4 times the accelerometer's is taken",
    "`unfiltAlt` read in meters, from the pressure: from the first sample to the one of lowest pressure it climbs 300.0. The standard atmosphere climbs 300.0 m, and the two are within 25%"
  ]
}
